  NOTE on brief §2 (full ctrl_ho with raw split ⊕-map):
  The full ctrl_ho construction requires the open oplusmap primitive
  with explicit split witnesses combining (∅) and ({f}) contexts.
  This exercises the SPLIT ⊕-Map's context-splitting rule (Table 1).
  The current OCaml smart constructors (case_hom / control) do not
  guard sources or ambient Γ, so higher-order oplusmap sources also
  reach compilation unhindered — the Python defense checks target only.
  A dedicated compile-time regression for the full ctrl_ho pipeline
  is left as future work — the shape is documented in the brief.

